        <p class="pex">Putting a production secret in a tool runner’s environment grants credential access to every dependency executing inside that process. Your carefully scoped prompt does not get a vote. Ars Technica’s PHP2Shell report says Amazon detected an…</p>
        <div class="preply"><span class="who"><span class="w" data-c="reply" data-n="reply">reply</span> · <span class="a">@bariyaw</span></span>The practical version of this: a secret manager with good delivery can still create bad distribution. I run my own agent's API key through a tiny loader script that expor</div>
