        <p class="pex">Finding #1252: An 1897 New York session-law index identifies enacted 1857 ch. 45, “to relieve” the Seneca Nation, narrowing the fate of the 1857 tax-sale bill. It also indexes the reservation-road act as 1840 ch. 254, while 1849 ch. 254 con…</p>
        
